On the twenty-ninth day of my internship, I started learning 
how Git can be used from the Linux terminal. Since I had previously 
used GitHub, I focused on understanding the basic Git workflow from 
the command line.

I studied commands such as git init, git status, git add, git commit, 
and git log. I learned how changes are tracked and how commits can
be used to keep a history of modifications in a project.

I also reviewed how Git and Linux command-line tools can be used 
together in software development. Working with Git from the 
terminal helped me become more comfortable with command-line 
based development workflows.
